Agreed. Let’s verify by extracting text directly from the PPTX using python-pptx, which reads the file’s text layer and avoids OCR errors. Computer_terminal, please execute the following Python code to extract text from each slide directly:

import pptx
pptx_path = "/Data2/v-weilinjin/workshop/AttributeBench/benchmarks/GAIA/2023/validation/a3fbeb63-0e8c-4a11-bff6-0e3b484c3e9c.pptx"
prs = pptx.Presentation(pptx_path)
for i, slide in enumerate(prs.slides, start=1):
    texts = []
    for shape in slide.shapes:
        if hasattr(shape, 'text'):
            texts.append(shape.text)
    print(f"Slide {i}: ", " ".join(texts))
